{"id": 35, "ts": 1780430185.4285953, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fB is our best choice after hearing Sarah\u2019s note that B can be \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d on top of the pretentiousness and occasional wrong tone we already knew about. Those traits raise serious doubts about crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014key safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011distance flights.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC demonstrates several core strengths: rapid, correct decision\u2011making; excellent attention to detail; and a clear orientation toward others\u2019 welfare, which suggests a collaborative mindset. While C does have difficulty communicating ideas and is seen as egocentric, the concern\u2011for\u2011others trait may mitigate the teamwork risk, and the communication issue could be addressed with targeted training.\nGiven the balance of strengths versus the more severe cooperation concerns for A, B, and D, I\u2019m shifting my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**. I\u2019d like to hear from James whether he has any observations on C\u2019s ability to work with crew members or his openness to feedback, to confirm whether the communication gap is manageable."}
