tion with other crew members.\n- **Stress resilience (interpersonal side) & adaptability:**\u202f\u201cCandidate\u202fD has a hot temper.\u201d A hot temper could affect calmness in high\u2011stress moments, especially when interacting with crew or ground personnel, and may limit openness to feedback or new ideas.\n**Overall assessment**\nCandidate\u202fD demonstrates the core technical and reliability attributes we need for long\u2011distance operations\u2014strong problem\u2011solving, focused attention, responsible judgment, and the ability to manage unexpected events. The concerns about a know\u2011it\u2011all attitude and occasional hot temper are notable, but they are outweighed by the concrete evidence of competence and responsibility. With appropriate crew\u2011resource\u2011management training and monitoring of interpersonal behavior, I believe Candidate\u202fD is the strongest overall fit for the position."}
